# How long a run may take in its mode, looked up in one table. `plans`, a `&HashMap<Mode, Plan>`, is one value: a map
# holds its values by its keys, and the key chooses the Plan the lookup `plans[&mode]` gives, as an index chooses an
# element of a slice; it is no value the table holds (#167). The route takes the table and the mode by their names,
# from its start, and reads both in its own code.

route tables.timeout
line entry > timeout call
line Plan·plans > timeout value              # `plans[&mode].timeout`
line Mode·mode > timeout value               # the key the lookup is made by

home Plan·plans timeout
home Mode·mode timeout

side entry left
